<BaseLayout title="Cooling System" description="Radiator, fans, IAT, and heater hose notes for LS Genesis Coupe swaps.">
  <h1>Cooling System</h1>
  <p>
    LS engines run hot in the Gen Coupe engine bay. Plan the cooling system early.
  </p>

  <h2>Key Points</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Plan a thick radiator and high-CFM fans early. LS engines run hot in the Gen Coupe bay.</li>
    <li>Oil cooler is strongly recommended, especially on higher-power or track cars.</li>
    <li>IAT sensor placement matters for accurate fueling — keep it in clean airflow, not heat-soaked.</li>
    <li>Holley Terminator X fan control can be set to not run on key-on (see the YouTube video linked on this page).</li>
  </ul>

